re\ncovered with water nearest to the river. Acorn, Hazelnut and Redbud\nroads are underwater with yards inundated.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 7:30 PM EST Wednesday the stage was 2.7 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 2.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 7:30 PM EST Wednesday was 2.8 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to remain steady above flood\nstage at 2.7 to 2.8 feet.\n- Flood stage is 2.3 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Thursday afternoon at noon EST.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSMLB"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS82 KMLB 120134"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KMLB.FL.W.0003.000000T0000Z-000000T0000Z/"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.505e8f7bcdba7736f6bbdd92a1fa13719b15a01e.001.1,2026-11-10T19:47:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e107256a42b0530b65688e8f07bafebc7c640d16.001.1,2026-11-10T09:29:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c9cf3f462f33a5e4d6ad2b4caef1b80879d8052b.001.1,2026-11-09T09:16:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4b285fc635ac6e22d5ca2389fc92c65dc81f18f7.001.1,2026-11-09T20:01:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9d2563c5250d1a21cbb48c4c8dde087f4dd19803.001.1,2026-11-09T11:56:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bf12750626b19b1d585cde97c9dd269cb2998e09.001.1,2026-11-08T10:53:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ace757809a48184dd60d7f2d82ec84e07516b042.001.1,2026-11-08T20:02:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c4