ia and Lake Counties.\n\n.Heavy rainfall has caused the St. Johns River near Deland to remain\njust below Minor Flood Stage. The river is forecast to remain nearly\nsteady into next week, but may slowly climb into Minor flood stage\nthis weekend.\n\nFor the St. Johns River...including Deland...Minor flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...St Johns River near Deland.\n\n* WHEN...Until Sunday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 4.0 feet, Docks and piers are completely submerged at\nPier 44 Marina. Many docks are partially submerged at Hontoon\nLanding Marina.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 7:30 PM EST Wednesday the stage was 3.9 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 3.5 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to a crest of 4.0 feet\nearly Friday afternoon. It will then fall below flood stage early\nSunday morning.\n- Flood stage is 4.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Motorists should not attempt to drive around barricades or drive cars\nthrough flooded areas.\n\nCaution is urged when walking near riverbanks.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued Thursday afternoon at noon EST.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSMLB"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS82 KMLB 120137"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL SUNDAY MORNING"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KMLB.FL.W.0005.000000T0000Z-261115T1200Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-11-15T07:00:00-05:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4aabaee6c5c98e5f31cb1f525643affd36388e4e.001.1,2026-11-10T19:47:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e4e3bf8c51e1f0d6d1aece7b6cc61a2b05ad487d.001.1,2026-11-10T09:26:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d956196ce32ccbfe40f51b57092a66a705fedab0.001.1,2026-11-09T09:19:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7f1defdc5ab7