ish River at Potlatch.\n\n* WHEN...Until early Thursday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 16.5 feet, the Skokomish River will cause widespread\nflooding of pasture lands, with water flowing quickly over West\nBourgault Road and Skokomish Valley Road.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 6:30 PM PST Wednesday the stage was 16.6 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 6:30 PM PST Wednesday was 17.6 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected subside below flood stage early\nThursday morning. The river will begin rising again Friday rising\nabove flood stage Friday afternoon and continue rising to a crest\nof 17.4 feet late Saturday morning.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued late tonight at 500 AM PST.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLSSEW"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS86 KSEW 120339"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING IN EFFECT THROUGH EARLY THURSDAY MORNING"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.KSEW.FL.W.0036.000000T0000Z-000000T0000Z/"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.568116e40631edf6192c77720da3efcfc4cbe192.001.1,2026-11-11T03:39:00-08:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4835cee124b4d700dba373eb190cec114e85bf46.001.1,2026-11-10T22:02:00-08:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5609965cd082440fb4cc153cfc1f4b8fdc50e756.001.1,2026-11-10T18:05:00-08:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FLS"],"NationalWeatherService":["FLW"]}}}]}